{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKHKUMep57cqAKGMe89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Prioritise fixing bank-connection failures, not streaks.**\n\n**Why not streaks:** A 12% DAU/MAU is probably fine for a budgeting app. Most people need to check their budget weekly, not daily. Streaks push for daily opens that don't match how people actually use the product, and push notifications could increase churn and opt-outs. The growth team's claim that engaged users retain better is a correlation; it doesn't show that pushing engagement causes retention.\n\n**Why connections:** Connecting a bank account is the clearest sign a user is getting value. The 3× retention gap is also partly selection, since motivated users connect anyway. But the 22% failure rate is different. Those users already tried to connect, and we're blocking them. Because the failures are concentrated at three banks, the work is narrow enough for two engineers in six weeks.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. **Week 1:** Break down the failures at those three banks by cause: aggregator errors, MFA or OAuth flows, timeouts, or user abandonment. Estimate how much of the failure rate each cause accounts for.\n2. **Weeks 2–5:** Fix the largest causes. Options include switching or adding an aggregator for those banks, OAuth migration, better retry and error messages, and saving progress so users can resume.\n3. **Throughout:** Add a recovery path for failed attempts, such as a \"try again\" email or push, or manual or CSV entry as a fallback. This is the one place notifications make clear sense.\n\n**Measure:** Connection success rate, the share of users who connect in week one (currently 34%), and 30-day retention as an early proxy for 90-day retention.\n\n**Check causality cheaply:** Compare users whose connection failed with similar users whose connection succeeded. Both groups showed the same intent, so the retention gap between them estimates how much a successful connection is actually worth. Use that to size the payoff before committing all six weeks."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3187,"cache_read_input_tokens":5030,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3187},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35157151-c85b-45aa-a0d5-922a6dfde5d7","uuid":"b43f26b9-c5bc-41aa-b66b-625bf9a37f58","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:25:39.899Z","request_id":"req_011CftKHKDya4BTDKo9xJkwA"}
